==Abstract==

This NEP defines a deterministic verification script for contract-based accounts.
The script embeds an opaque <code>accountId</code> and a verifier contract hash, calls <code>verify(accountId)</code> on that contract, and uses the script hash of the verification script as the public account address.

==Motivation==

Neo contracts can already verify witnesses, but wallets, SDKs, explorers, RPC tooling, and relayers need a common script shape to recognize contract-based accounts, estimate verification costs, construct signing contexts, and derive addresses consistently.
Without a standard verification script, different implementations may assign different addresses to the same logical contract-based account or make different assumptions about the invocation script required for verification.

Abstract Accounts are one possible use case for this standard because they can derive account addresses without deploying a new contract for every user.
The standard itself is not limited to Abstract Accounts and does not define an account storage model, ownership model, or execution model.

This NEP standardizes only the witness verification script and the address derived from it.

==Specification==

===Terms===

* <code>accountId</code>: an opaque <code>ByteString</code> identifying one account within the verifier contract.
* <code>verifierContract</code>: the <code>Hash160</code> of the contract that decides whether the account witness is valid.
* <code>accountAddress</code>: the script hash of the verification script defined by this NEP.

===Verification script===

A compliant contract-based account verification script MUST be semantically equivalent to:

<pre>
System.Contract.Call(verifierContract, "verify", ReadOnly, [accountId])
</pre>

The verification script:

* MUST embed <code>accountId</code> as a constant.
* MUST embed <code>verifierContract</code> as a constant.
* MUST call the method named <code>verify</code> on <code>verifierContract</code>.
* MUST pass only <code>accountId</code> to <code>verify</code>.
* MUST use the <code>ReadOnly</code> call flag.
* MUST return the Boolean result of that call.

The verifier contract's <code>verify</code> method:

* MUST accept one <code>ByteString</code> argument.
* MUST return a Boolean value.
* MUST NOT require an invocation script for the standard account witness.

===Address derivation===

The public address of a contract-based account compliant with this NEP MUST be the script hash of the full verification script defined above.

Wallets, SDKs, explorers, indexers, RPC tooling, and relayers:

* MUST derive the account address from the full verification script.
* MUST NOT derive the address from <code>accountId</code> alone.
* SHOULD use this script shape to identify compliant contract-based account witnesses.

===Witness rules===

When a transaction uses a contract-based account address defined by this NEP as a signer:

* the witness verification script MUST be the deterministic verification script for that account;
* the invocation script SHOULD be empty;
* authorization MUST be decided by the verifier contract's <code>verify(accountId)</code> method.

===Out of scope===

This NEP does not standardize:

* how <code>accountId</code> is created;
* how the verifier contract stores account state;
* how application execution happens after verification succeeds;
* whether an account is transferable;
* metadata for accounts;
* native signatures, meta-transactions, or custom verifier schemes.

==Rationale==

The goal of this NEP is minimal interoperability.
It provides one canonical witness script shape for contract-based account addresses while leaving account policy and execution logic to separate contracts and, if needed, separate standards.

By tying the account address to a deterministic script instead of a deployed per-account contract, this approach allows implementations to avoid per-account deployment while preserving normal Neo witness verification semantics.

==Backwards Compatibility==

Existing contract-based account systems that use another script format can continue to work, but they are not compliant with this NEP and will not derive the same address for the same <code>accountId</code> and <code>verifierContract</code>.

==Implementation==

The <code>neo-abstract-account</code> repository contains one implementation of this script pattern in <code>sdk/js/src/index.js</code>.
